 html←GetStatisticsDownloads(folder list);filename;size
⍝ Returns the "Downloads" tab of the usage data page; see `GetStatistics`.
⍝ The links are absolute: relative to "/v1/usage-data" they would end up in the REST route.
 html←⊂'<section class="tab-panel" id="download" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-download">'
 html,←⊂'<h3 class="tab-title">Downloads</h3>'
 html,←⊂'<ul class="download-list">'
 :For filename :In list
     size←1⌈⌊0.5+(2 ⎕NINFO folder,filename)÷1024       ⍝ ⎕NINFO property 2 is the size in bytes
     html,←⊂'<li><a href="/usage-data/',filename,'">Data for ',(UsageDataPeriod filename),'</a><span>zip, about ',(⍕size),' KB</span></li>'
 :EndFor
 html,←⊂'</ul>'
 html,←⊂'</section>'
⍝Done
